<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico drained 4.078 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and seven repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    360 days   23.10 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    178 days   22.32 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days   22.09 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     43 days   22.59 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     35 days   22.28 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     30 days   22.00 pct</p>
<p>    550 million     18 days   22.25 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     11 days   22.88 pct</p>
<p>    800 million	3 days   22.97 pct</p>
<p>    178 million	1 day    22.83 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
